  "limitations": [
    "This qualifies native FRI proofs over synthetic hidden committed inputs. It does not qualify complete wallet/recursive STARK proofs, the hiding PCS opening wrapper, backend selection, all proving stages or worker/pool integration.",
    "No performance or transaction-throughput measurement is claimed for this checkpoint.",
    "Only the desktop RTX 5080 executed CUDA tests. V100, multi-device ownership rejection and Metal execution remain unqualified; existing NVRTC tests still compile compute_70 and compute_120 kernels.",
    "The intentional missing-kernel API-error test runs outside sanitizers. All five opt-in primitive benchmarks are excluded from correctness/sanitizer runs.",
    "The exact wire comparisons use zero-PoW test settings because upstream parallel grinding may choose a different valid witness. Production-PoW proofs are checked by the unmodified CPU verifier."
  ],
  "qualification_note": "All 771 source files were frozen for qualification and stream checks and match staged Git blobs. Development logs preserve API-path/type fixes and the discovered query-staging census correction. A new no-fold fixture initially assumed nonzero preprocessing rows stayed constant; preprocessing interleaves zeros, so the final zero-polynomial fixture states the actual constant case. A same-device foreign-runtime test encountered the required exclusive GPU lease and was removed without weakening the lease or claiming multi-device coverage. Development run 06 passed all seven protocol tests. The final 37-check qualification and 17-test stream run passed without retries. Ordinary tests use a 3 GiB cap; the stream build used a 6 GiB cap and one build job. All services prohibit swap and limit CPU use to four threads.",
